        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.331,
            0.106
          ],
          "content": "**Aditya’s method:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.106,
            0.6,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": "The required area is 2 times the area of JKLM."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.341,
            0.133,
            0.514,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{JK} = \\frac{X - y}{2}, \\mathrm{KM} = x",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.169,
            0.383,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "Area $( \\mathrm { { J K M L } } ) = x \\left( { \\frac { x - y } { 2 } } \\right)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.202,
            0.48,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": "Required area = 2 × Area of JKML = 2x (x – y) 2 = x (x – y)."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.722,
            0.078,
            0.901,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.281,
            0.847,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": "? By expanding the expressions, verify that all three expressions are equivalent. If $x = 8  and  y = 3.$ , find the area of the shaded region."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.337,
            0.803,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": "？ Write an expression for the area of the dashed region in the figure below. Use more than one method to arrive at the answer. Substitute $p = 6,   r = 3.5,$ , and $s = 9$ , and calculate the area."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.815,
            0.328,
            0.904,
            0.381
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.39,
            0.411,
            0.607,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.575,
            0.293,
            0.598
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.6,
            0.701,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": "1. Compute these products using the suggested identity."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.624,
            0.56,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": "(i) $4 6 ^ { 2 }$ using Identity 1A for $( a + b ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.649,
            0.673,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $3 9 7 \\times 4 0 3$ using Identity 1C for $\\left( a + b \\right) \\left( a - b \\right)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.672,
            0.557,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $9 1 ^ { 2 }$ using Identity 1B for $( a - b ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.697,
            0.651,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": "(iv) $4 3 \\times 4 5$ using Identity 1C for $( a + b )   ( a - b )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.721,
            0.846,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": "2. Use either a suitable identity or the distributive property to find each of the following products."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.763,
            0.389,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "(i) $(p - 1)(p + 11)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.787,
            0.422,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $( 3 a - 9 b ) ( 3 a + 9 b )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.812,
            0.41,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $-(2y+5)\\left ( 3y+4 \\right )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.835,
            0.343,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": "(iv) $( 6 x + 5 y ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.863,
            0.332,
            0.887
          ],
          "content": "(v) $( 2 X   -   { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.888,
            0.429,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": "$( 7 p ) \\times ( 3 r ) \\times ( p + 2 )$"
        },
        {
